replies.text:
I'll analyze EVAL-03 and build the threat model based on the context provided.

Looking at this design, I see several critical security issues:

**Key Concerns:**
- Health data cached unencrypted on shared tablets
- No session management between shift changes  
- Offline access with no authorization checks
- Physical device security risks

Here's the complete threat model:

```json
{
  "schema": "redline.threatmodel.v1",
  "issueKey": "EVAL-03",
  "sketch": {
    "components": ["Tablet app", "SQLite database", "Offline cache", "Sync service"],
    "dataStores": ["SQLite database"],
    "externalServices": [],
    "trustBoundaries": ["Device boundary", "Shift boundary"],
    "dataClasses": ["health"],
    "exposure": "internal",
    "llmFeatures": false
  },
  "threats": [
    {
      "stride": "InformationDisclosure",
      "title": "Unencrypted patient data exposed on shared tablet",
      "scenario": "A nurse picks up a shared tablet and directly accesses the SQLite database file (using adb, file browser, or backup tools) to read all cached patient notes and medical history from previous shifts, including patients they should not have access to.",
      "component": "SQLite database",
      "likelihood": 5,
      "impact": 5,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "Devices are shared between shifts"
        },
        {
          "quote": "caches patient notes and medical history offline in a local SQLite database"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": [],
      "cwe": ["CWE-311", "CWE-312"],
      "plainLanguage": "Anyone who picks up the tablet can read all patient records stored on it",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Encrypt local patient data",
        "given": "patient notes and medical history are cached offline",
        "when": "data is written to the SQLite database",
        "then": "it must be encrypted using platform-provided encryption (Android EncryptedSharedPreferences or iOS Data Protection API)"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "Spoofing",
      "title": "Previous nurse's session remains active on shared device",
      "scenario": "Nurse A ends their shift and hands the tablet to Nurse B without logging out. Nurse B continues using the app under Nurse A's identity, accessing patients and making notes that appear to come from Nurse A.",
      "component": "Tablet app",
      "likelihood": 4,
      "impact": 4,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "Devices are shared between shifts"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": ["V3.3.1"],
      "cwe": ["CWE-613"],
      "plainLanguage": "The next nurse can keep using the previous nurse's login if they don't log out",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Force logout between shifts",
        "given": "devices are shared between shifts",
        "when": "a shift ends or device ownership changes",
        "then": "the app must require reauthentication and clear the previous session"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "InformationDisclosure",
      "title": "Patient records linger after shift change",
      "scenario": "Nurse A caches 20 patient records during their shift. When Nurse B starts, the app still displays those patients in search results, recent lists, or cached queries, exposing patients Nurse B should not access.",
      "component": "Offline cache",
      "likelihood": 5,
      "impact": 4,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "Devices are shared between shifts"
        },
        {
          "quote": "caches patient notes and medical history offline"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": [],
      "cwe": ["CWE-284"],
      "plainLanguage": "The new nurse can see patient records from the previous nurse's shift",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Clear cached data on session change",
        "given": "devices are shared between shifts",
        "when": "a nurse logs out or a new nurse logs in",
        "then": "all cached patient data from the previous session must be purged"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "ElevationOfPrivilege",
      "title": "Nurse accesses patients beyond their authorization",
      "scenario": "The app caches all patient records a nurse queries. Because offline access control is not enforced (only assignment, unit, or authorization are checked during sync), a nurse can search for and access any patient previously cached on the device, even those outside their care assignment.",
      "component": "Offline cache",
      "likelihood": 4,
      "impact": 4,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "caches patient notes and medical history offline in a local SQLite database"
        },
        {
          "quote": "work without signal"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": ["V4.1.1"],
      "cwe": ["CWE-284"],
      "plainLanguage": "Nurses can look up and read notes for any patient previously loaded on the tablet",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Enforce access control offline",
        "given": "nurses work without signal",
        "when": "a nurse attempts to access a cached patient record",
        "then": "the app must verify offline that the nurse is authorized (by unit, role, or explicit assignment) and refuse access otherwise"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "Tampering",
      "title": "Direct modification of offline database bypasses validation",
      "scenario": "A malicious user with device access (or adb) opens the SQLite file and changes patient notes, diagnosis codes, or medication records. When the app syncs, it uploads the tampered data without verifying integrity.",
      "component": "SQLite database",
      "likelihood": 2,
      "impact": 5,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "local SQLite database"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": [],
      "cwe": ["CWE-353"],
      "plainLanguage": "Someone with device access can alter patient records before they sync",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Integrity-protect offline data",
        "given": "patient data is cached in a local SQLite database",
        "when": "data is written or synced",
        "then": "the app must sign or HMAC each record and reject any that fail verification"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "Repudiation",
      "title": "Offline actions cannot be audited",
      "scenario": "While offline, a nurse views or edits patient records. These actions are not logged with timestamp, user, and patient ID. Later, when investigating a privacy breach or malpractice claim, there is no evidence of who accessed what while offline.",
      "component": "Offline cache",
      "likelihood": 4,
      "impact": 3,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "work without signal"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": [],
      "cwe": ["CWE-778"],
      "plainLanguage": "No record exists of who accessed which patient files while offline",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Queue audit events offline",
        "given": "nurses work without signal",
        "when": "a nurse views or modifies a patient record offline",
        "then": "the app must log the action locally (nurse ID, patient ID, action, timestamp) and sync audit logs when connectivity returns"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "InformationDisclosure",
      "title": "Stolen or lost tablet exposes patient data",
      "scenario": "A tablet is left in a taxi or stolen from a hospital locker. The attacker boots the device, enables USB debugging or pulls the SQLite file from backup, and extracts all cached patient notes and medical history.",
      "component": "Tablet app",
      "likelihood": 3,
      "impact": 5,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "tablet app"
        },
        {
          "quote": "caches patient notes and medical history offline in a local SQLite database"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": [],
      "cwe": ["CWE-311"],
      "plainLanguage": "If the tablet is lost, all patient records on it can be read by whoever finds it",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Require device security baseline",
        "given": "tablets cache health data",
        "when": "the app starts",
        "then": "it must verify device encryption is enabled, screen lock is set, and refuse to cache data if these protections are missing"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "Tampering",
      "title": "Malicious sync overwrites legitimate patient data",
      "scenario": "A nurse modifies patient notes offline. Another nurse, using the same tablet in a different shift, also modifies the same patient offline (cached from an earlier sync). Both changes sync, and the last one wins, silently discarding the earlier nurse's updates.",
      "component": "Sync service",
      "likelihood": 3,
      "impact": 4,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "Offline sync"
        },
        {
          "quote": "Devices are shared between shifts"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": [],
      "cwe": ["CWE-662"],
      "plainLanguage": "Two nurses editing the same record offline can cause one person's changes to be lost",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Detect and resolve sync conflicts",
        "given": "multiple nurses may edit the same patient offline",
        "when": "the app syncs changes",
        "then": "it must detect conflicts (e.g., via version numbers or timestamps) and either merge intelligently or prompt for manual resolution instead of silently overwriting"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
